{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.CocenterTraceFactor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.CocenterTraceFactor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Quotient.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTraceCyclicity"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.traceCocenter_End","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.traceCocenter_End","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CocenterTraceFactor.lean#L132-L143","doc":"**The Markov-trace model: `LinearMap.trace` factors through the cocenter of\n`End V` (sorry-free).**  The trace's commutation `trace(fg) = trace(gf)`\n(`trace_mul_comm`) is exactly `IsCyclic`, so `tr_M` descends to\n`HH₀(End V)` — the `HH₀`-level form of `MagnitudeTraceCommutator`'s\n`trace_comp_conjOp`.  The decision information the trace discards is the\ncomplementary `[End V, End V]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_trace_of_separates_commutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_trace_of_separates_commutator","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CocenterTraceFactor.lean#L113-L130","doc":"**Any functional separating a commutator-difference is a NON-trace\n(sorry-free).**  The contrapositive of `trace_eq_of_sub_mem_commutator`: if\n`φ` distinguishes `a, b` with `a − b ∈ [A,A]`, then `φ` is *not* cyclic — the\nconclusion `∃ x y, φ(xy) ≠ φ(yx)` is exactly `¬ IsCyclic ⇑φ`.\n\nThis is the precise, **proved** form of the P-vs-NP wall's necessary\ncondition: a **decision residue** must separate the `[A,A]` (decision) axis,\nso it is necessarily a **non-trace** — a class in `HH₁`, not `HH₀`, and in\nparticular *not* any Euler-characteristic / `K₀` invariant (`χ = −6`). The\nresidue's remaining requirement — that such a non-trace `φ` be\n**non-algebraic** (efficiently uncomputable) — is the algebrization barrier\n(Aaronson–Wigderson), which lives outside this algebraic statement and keeps\n`res ≠ 0` open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.trace_add_commutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.trace_add_commutator","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CocenterTraceFactor.lean#L106-L111","doc":"**Adding a commutator does not move a trace (sorry-free).**  `τ(x + (ab − ba))\n= τ x` — the infinitesimal form of trace-blindness on the `[A,A]` axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.trace_eq_of_sub_mem_commutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.trace_eq_of_sub_mem_commutator","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CocenterTraceFactor.lean#L96-L104","doc":"**A trace is blind to `[A,A]`-differences (sorry-free).**  If `a − b ∈ [A,A]`\nthen `τ a = τ b`: no trace (hence no `K₀`/Euler-characteristic invariant)\ndistinguishes elements that differ by a sum of commutators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.traceCocenter_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.traceCocenter_mk","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CocenterTraceFactor.lean#L81-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.traceCocenter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.traceCocenter","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CocenterTraceFactor.lean#L73-L79","doc":"**A trace factors through the cocenter (sorry-free).**  A cyclic `τ` descends\nto a linear functional on `HH₀(A) = A/[A,A]`: the magnitude functional is a\nfunction of the cocenter class alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.commutatorSubmodule_le_ker_of_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.commutatorSubmodule_le_ker_of_trace","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CocenterTraceFactor.lean#L62-L71","doc":"**A trace functional kills `[A,A]` (sorry-free).**  Any linear `τ` that is\n`IsCyclic` (`τ(ab) = τ(ba)`) vanishes on every generator `a·b − b·a`, hence on\ntheir span `[A,A]`. The hypothesis is the shared\n`Machinery.BilinearTrace.IsCyclic` predicate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.cocenter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.cocenter","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CocenterTraceFactor.lean#L57-L58","doc":"The **cocenter** `HH₀(A) = A / [A,A]` — the target of every trace functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.commutatorSubmodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.commutatorSubmodule","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CocenterTraceFactor.lean#L53-L55","doc":"The **commutator submodule** `[A,A]` — the `R`-span of all `a·b − b·a`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}